# brand-studio
#
# Rule of thumb: build OUTPUT is disposable and stays out; brand INPUT is the
# product and stays in. A deck or a film can always be rebuilt from its IR plus
# the brand profile — a logo, a font or a reference cut cannot be rebuilt from
# anything.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   brands/*/assets/**      logos, fonts, token dumps — shipped brand assets
#   brands/*/video/**       supplied intro/outro plates, music beds, reference films
#   examples/*.json         the worked Deck IR and Video IR examples
#   grammar/icons/*.svg     the shared icon set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
examples/**/*.pptx
examples/**/*.mp4
examples/**/*.pdf
examples/**/*.srt
examples/**/*.timeline.json
examples/out/
out/

# Any directory literally named out/ or preview/, at any depth, plus the
# <deck>.preview/ directories render_preview.sh drops beside a deck.
**/out/
**/preview/
*.preview/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# render intermediates
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build_video.py work dirs, frame sequences, per-scene HTML and Chrome profiles.
**/frames/
**/chrome-profiles/
.brand-studio-work/
*.brand-studio-work/
tmp/
.tmp/
*.tmp

# macOS 'say' writes AIFF before it is normalised into the mix.
*.aiff
*.aif

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# office lock files, left behind by soffice and PowerPoint
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.~lock.*#
~$*.pptx
~$*.docx
~$*.xlsx

# Nightly review packets are generated output: they carry absolute paths from the
# machine that built them and would churn on every run. The learning that must be
# shared lives in LEARNED.md, rules.local.json and daily/metrics.json, all tracked.
brands/*/daily/*/
!brands/*/daily/metrics.json

# Generated music beds (regenerated deterministically from a seed).
brands/*/audio/generated/
